WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.233 --> 00:00:16.602
"You found the spot where the treasure is buried?"

2
00:00:16.942 --> 00:00:18.123
Cole ran toward Maggie.

3
00:00:19.024 --> 00:00:20.745
Henry and the others rushed after him.

4
00:00:21.766 --> 00:00:24.168
Even Roger wandered over, looking curious.

5
00:00:25.148 --> 00:00:26.749
Maggie was still digging in the sand.

6
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.852
Cole, Henry, Nathan, and Luke joined in.

7
00:00:30.948 --> 00:00:33.049
Soon they uncovered a large wooden trunk.

8
00:00:33.069 --> 00:00:36.009
"It looks like a real pirate chest!"

9
00:00:36.429 --> 00:00:37.130
Nathan said.

10
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:38.570
He looked at Roger.

11
00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:39.630
"Doesn't it?"

12
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.111
"Sure does."

13
00:00:41.511 --> 00:00:42.231
Roger winked.

14
00:00:42.951 --> 00:00:44.352
"Have fun with your treasure, kids.

15
00:00:45.252 --> 00:00:47.512
But watch out for Roger Redbeard!"

16
00:00:50.253 --> 00:00:51.634
He wandered off, whistling.

17
00:00:51.654 --> 00:00:54.574
"What are we waiting for, you guys?"

18
00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:55.895
Cole said eagerly.

19
00:00:55.915 --> 00:00:58.335
"Let's find out what our booty is!"

20
00:00:59.656 --> 00:01:00.816
Maggie opened the trunk.

21
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:03.600
"Pirate hats!"

22
00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:04.881
she said.

23
00:01:04.902 --> 00:01:07.183
Luke grabbed one and then handed another one to Henry.

24
00:01:07.203 --> 00:01:10.186
"This one has your name on it, Henry."

25
00:01:12.207 --> 00:01:13.588
Cole pulled out more hats.

26
00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:16.731
"We each have one."

27
00:01:17.672 --> 00:01:19.593
Nathan grinned and put on his hat.

28
00:01:19.613 --> 00:01:21.455
"Do I look like a pirate?"

29
00:01:22.436 --> 00:01:23.216
Anna snorted.

30
00:01:23.236 --> 00:01:27.019
"You look like a kid with a dumb hat on to me," she said.

31
00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.821
Laughing, she tried her hat on too.

32
00:01:30.702 --> 00:01:32.724
Henry put on his hat and glanced at William.

33
00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:34.813
William hadn't touched his hat.

34
00:01:35.693 --> 00:01:40.355
And instead of laughing at how silly everyone looked, William had an angry scowl on his face.

35
00:01:41.496 --> 00:01:42.816
Henry moved closer to Cole.

36
00:01:43.276 --> 00:01:46.478
"Did you notice how strange William is acting today?"

37
00:01:46.858 --> 00:01:47.458
he whispered.

38
00:01:47.478 --> 00:01:50.239
"No." Cole glanced toward William.

39
00:01:50.259 --> 00:01:51.400
"What do you mean?"

40
00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:56.742
"He doesn't seem very excited about this treasure hunt," Henry whispered.

41
00:01:56.762 --> 00:02:00.584
"Do you think it's because he helped his parents hide the booty?

42
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.582
Maybe he's trying not to give us any hints."

43
00:02:03.602 --> 00:02:06.164
"Maybe." Cole shrugged.

44
00:02:06.184 --> 00:02:10.808
"Or maybe he's bored because he does cool stuff like this all the time.

45
00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:13.490
His family is really rich, remember?"

46
00:02:13.831 --> 00:02:14.571
Cole went on.

47
00:02:14.591 --> 00:02:17.814
"They might have fancy treasure hunts every weekend."

48
00:02:18.835 --> 00:02:22.898
Meanwhile Luke had spotted a folded-up piece of paper inside the treasure chest.

49
00:02:23.999 --> 00:02:26.141
"I think this is our next clue," he said.

50
00:02:27.942 --> 00:02:29.504
Maggie unfolded the piece of paper.

51
00:02:30.128 --> 00:02:32.649
It was a drawing of a blue object along the beach.

52
00:02:32.669 --> 00:02:35.390
"What do you think this is supposed to be?"

53
00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:36.410
she murmured.

54
00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.110
"A swimming pool?"

55
00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:39.031
said Cole.

56
00:02:39.051 --> 00:02:42.572
"It looks like a little pond," said Henry.

57
00:02:42.592 --> 00:02:44.532
"Or a tide pool!"

58
00:02:44.892 --> 00:02:45.412
said Anna.

59
00:02:45.432 --> 00:02:47.073
"I bet that's what it is."

60
00:02:49.113 --> 00:02:50.274
Luke glanced around the beach.

61
00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:57.116
the closest one?"

62
00:02:57.396 --> 00:02:57.936
he asked.

63
00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.622
"Hmm Anna said, thinking.

64
00:03:01.642 --> 00:03:04.644
"There are at least four tide pools near here.

65
00:03:05.145 --> 00:03:06.906
We should split up and check all of them."

66
00:03:06.926 --> 00:03:10.169
"Nathan and I will search together," Luke said.

67
00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:12.871
"I'll go with Henry," Maggie said.

68
00:03:12.891 --> 00:03:15.113
"Okay," Anna said.

69
00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:18.616
"I can search alone, since I know this beach better than anyone else."

70
00:03:18.636 --> 00:03:22.659
"I guess that leaves you and me," Cole told William with a grin.

71
00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.122
Anna told each pair where to go.

72
00:03:25.802 --> 00:03:27.784
Then the kids set out in different directions.

73
00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:36.130
It took Henry and Maggie about half an hour to find their tide pool and look for the

74
00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.932
treasure. But they didn't find anything.

75
00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:43.434
"Let's go see if the others found the treasure," Maggie said.

76
00:03:47.857 --> 00:03:49.717
They returned to the beach in front of the house.

77
00:03:50.398 --> 00:03:51.398
Cole was already there.

78
00:03:51.418 --> 00:03:53.319
"Did you find the booty?"

79
00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:54.500
Maggie asked him.

80
00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.621
"Nope," Cole said.

81
00:03:56.641 --> 00:03:57.562
"Did you?"

82
00:03:58.642 --> 00:03:59.643
Henry shook his head.

83
00:03:59.663 --> 00:04:01.003
"Where's William?"

84
00:04:01.344 --> 00:04:01.844
he asked.

85
00:04:02.772 --> 00:04:05.713
"William left right after we all split up," Cole replied.

86
00:04:05.733 --> 00:04:07.934
"He said he had to use the bathroom.

87
00:04:08.395 --> 00:04:09.395
But he never came back."

88
00:04:10.275 --> 00:04:11.896
Cole frowned, looking annoyed.

89
00:04:11.916 --> 00:04:14.777
"I had to find our tide pool all by myself."

90
00:04:15.758 --> 00:04:18.799
Before Henry could respond, he saw Anna walking toward them.

91
00:04:18.819 --> 00:04:20.720
"No luck, huh?"

92
00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:21.640
she asked.

93
00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:22.861
"Me neither."

94
00:04:23.861 --> 00:04:25.442
Just then they all heard a shout.

95
00:04:26.042 --> 00:04:26.722
It was Nathan.

96
00:04:27.283 --> 00:04:29.924
He was racing down the beach toward them, waving his arms.

97
00:04:30.956 --> 00:04:31.677
"We found it!"

98
00:04:32.017 --> 00:04:32.558
he cried.

99
00:04:33.098 --> 00:04:35.821
He skidded to a stop and then bent over to catch his breath.

100
00:04:36.441 --> 00:04:37.602
He started coughing.

101
00:04:38.243 --> 00:04:39.905
"Take it easy," Cole said.

102
00:04:39.925 --> 00:04:41.526
"Did you say you found the booty?"

103
00:04:43.208 --> 00:04:43.968
Nathan nodded.

104
00:04:44.569 --> 00:04:49.514
When he finally stopped coughing, he said, "Luke and I had some trouble finding our tide pool.

105
00:04:50.394 --> 00:04:53.918
But when we got there, we spotted something in the water right away.

106
00:04:54.919 --> 00:04:56.060
Come on, I'll show you."

107
00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.803
Henry, Maggie, Anna, and Cole followed him down the beach.

108
00:05:01.944 --> 00:05:04.526
When they reached Nathan's tide pool, Maggie gasped.

109
00:05:04.546 --> 00:05:08.189
"It's tear-shaped—like the picture on the map!"

110
00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:11.471
Luke was fishing a plastic container out of the water.

111
00:05:12.132 --> 00:05:13.933
William was there, watching him.

112
00:05:13.954 --> 00:05:15.995
"Is that the treasure?"

113
00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:18.097
Maggie wondered, eying the box.

114
00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.798
"It's pretty small."

115
00:05:19.818 --> 00:05:22.761
"Open it," Nathan urged.

116
00:05:23.741 --> 00:05:25.083
Luke opened the container.

117
00:05:25.623 --> 00:05:26.444
Then he frowned.

118
00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.182
"This can't be the treasure."

119
00:05:28.202 --> 00:05:29.524
"Why not?"

120
00:05:29.885 --> 00:05:30.646
Henry asked.

121
00:05:30.666 --> 00:05:32.128
"What's wrong?"

122
00:05:36.154 --> 00:05:38.678
Luke held the container out so they could all see inside.

123
00:05:38.698 --> 00:05:42.184
"There's nothing in here except a few soggy sticks of gum!"
